/-- Explicit power-associated-prime input for \(I_a\), needed because Mathlib and Proposition 2.1
currently expose associated primes only for a `HasComponents` family of pure-power ideals, not for
powers of those components. This hypothesis starts at exponent two; exponent one is proved below. -/
def prop62_hasWeightedPowerAssociatedPrimes (B : ι → Finset σ) (a : σ → ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ q : ℕ, 2 ≤ q →
    associatedPrimes (MvPolynomial σ K)
        (MvPolynomial σ K ⧸ prop62_weightedIdeal (K := K) B a ^ q) =
      Set.range (fun h : ι ↦ (primeOf (B h) : Ideal (MvPolynomial σ K)))

